     7	    python3 mapping.py result <out folder>                 # mapping.json: covers true / false / "split" per matter and question; distinct bets
     8	
     9	Covers: both families mark the question `opened`, or `narrower` with both saying it carries the matter's main outcome. A question one family
    10	marks covering and the other not goes to two third readers; covering when both say yes, not covering when both say no, otherwise "split".
    11	A duplicate is the later-opened question of a same-bet pair; "duplicates_both" counts those both families mark, "duplicates_split" those one
    12	marks. Which question of a named pair is the later one is decided by code from the library's opening order, not by the reader.
    13	
    14	Ids: each library is exported with neutral ids Q1..Qn in opening order (the system's own ids differ in form between the systems); the
    15	system's id is kept as `source_id` beside it, and the guardrail sample draws from the system's ids as the frozen rule says (D675).
