     1	"""The council's marking of the comparison cards (verdict-rule.json marks, controls; card-spec.md; Deck 1's protocol; D672). Every session is
     2	closed (census_readers.run); no session sees the key, which is kept outside the repository.
     3	
     4	    python3 mark_cards.py deck <mapping out> <deck folder>     # covering cards, the guardrail sample, the controls; shuffled, keyed
     5	    python3 mark_cards.py mark <deck folder>                   # both families mark every card
     6	    python3 mark_cards.py debate <deck folder> <round>         # rounds 1 and 2 on every card whose marks differ
     7	    python3 mark_cards.py readings <mapping out> <deck folder> # readings.json for score_comparison.py
     8	
     9	Marks: worth (worth / trivia / duplicate); answer (supported / unsupported / insufficient), not asked on a card with no answer. A mark still
    10	split after two rounds is {"split": [codex mark, claude mark]}. A debate round reads only the rounds before it and resends the whole brief
    11	(closed sessions remember nothing); a round is complete only when every mark it owes is written (`round-N.done`), and readings refuse a deck
    12	whose three rounds are not complete. The guardrail sample draws from the system's own ids (`source_id`), sorted as strings (verdict-rule.json).
    13	"""
    14	import concurrent.futures
    15	import json
    16	import random
    17	import sys
    18	from pathlib import Path
    19	
    20	HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
    21	sys.path[:0] = [str(HERE), str(HERE / 'census')]
    22	import build_cards  # noqa: E402
    23	import census_readers  # noqa: E402
    24	from census_merge import json_lines  # noqa: E402
    25	import mapping as mapping_tool  # noqa: E402
    26	
    27	FAMILIES = census_readers.FAMILIES
    28	SEED = 20261117
    29	KEY = mapping_tool.KEY_FOLDER / 'deck-key.json'
    30	WORTH = ('worth', 'trivia', 'duplicate')
    31	ANSWER = ('supported', 'unsupported', 'insufficient')
    32	
    33	BRIEF = """You are a senior hedge-fund analyst who follows NVIDIA. You are reviewing one card from a research library's output as it stood on 20
    34	September 2026. Everything you may use is in this message. Do not read any file or run any command. Some cards in the deck are controls. Mark
    35	the card on its own merits.
    36	
    37	The house standard for what is worth tracking (quoted): "A question is a bet an analyst would hold a card for: a big matter, never trivia (a
    38	deal, product or project opens one only when its scale can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk). Small matters open no question …
    39	wordings, deadlines, milestones and periods of one bet are one question." "Most of what an item says is noise … new information that changes
    40	an answer is never missed."
    41	
    42	Mark:
    43	1. `worth`: "Is this a question worth tracking for this company?" Answer worth, trivia, or duplicate (duplicate only when an earlier-opened
    44	   question in the same library listed on the card is the same bet: the same outcome settles both and their answers cannot move apart).
    45	2. `answer` (only when the card shows a latest answer): "Is the latest answer supported by the material it was given?" Answer supported,
    46	   unsupported (the material points to another answer, or the answer contradicts its reasons or material), or insufficient (the material is
    47	   too thin to choose any answer). Judge whether the reasons and the material justify the chosen answer over its neighbours.
    48	3. `why`: one or two sentences naming what decides your marks.
    49	
    50	Return one JSON object and nothing else: {{"worth": "...", "answer": "..." or null, "why": "..."}}
    51	
    52	## The card
    53	
    54	{card}
    55	"""
    56	
    57	DEBATE = """
    58	
    59	## A second look
    60	
    61	You marked this card before; another reader marked it differently. Read the card again, your mark and reason, and the other reader's, against
    62	the definitions above. Keep or change each disputed mark, with a reason. Return one JSON object and nothing else: {{"worth": "...", "answer":
    63	"..." or null, "why": "..."}}
    64	
    65	Your mark: {own}
    66	The other reader's mark: {other}
    67	"""
    68	
    69	CONFIRM = """You are a senior hedge-fund analyst who follows NVIDIA. Is the latest answer on this card supported by the material it was
    70	given? Judge whether the reasons and the material justify the chosen answer over its neighbours. Return one JSON object and nothing else:
    71	{{"supported": true|false, "why": "<= 30 words"}}
    72	
    73	## The card
    74	
    75	{card}
    76	"""
