  9685	  - the debate prompt did not resend the marks' definitions to closed sessions, and could read a mark of its own round; readings could
  9686	    skip the debate;
  9687	  - a plant could land on a one-rung ladder; the deck's shuffle seed differed from the card spec's;
  9688	  - the card labelled the speaker as the publisher and cut quotes at their first line break (829 stored judge requests of both systems now
  9689	    parse to their stated item counts, 248 items with line breaks kept whole, 59 speakers holding a semicolon).
