  9483	  4. **One ledger per draw.**
  9484	     - Absolute guards: $65 per new-system draw and $25 per old-system draw, $270 in all. They are stops, not a budget (D664).
  9485	     - For this run, this replaces D449's whole-run stop across draws and D666's single $250 ledger. D449's one redo within a draw is
  9486	       unchanged.
  9487	  5. **D431's "same day," for a run longer than one day.** A new-system draw takes about 20 h, so one calendar day cannot hold it.
  9488	     - The six counted draws are launched within one hour of each other and run concurrently.
  9489	     - A redo within a draw counts as part of that draw.
  9490	     - Every counted send falls within 72 h of the first launch.
  9491	     - A breach makes the result a diagnostic.
  9492	     - This replaces, for this run only, the one-calendar-day reading in `WIRING-DESIGN.md`.
  9493	  6. **No replacement draw counts.** A draw that cannot finish gives no release verdict; what finished goes to Alex as a diagnostic. The
  9494	     reviewers read "same day" differently, so the council took the cheaper, reversible course (D439).
  9495	  7. **The credit and scoring rules** are plan §1.4:
    27	
    28	def item_lookup(items_db):
    29	    """input id → title, publisher and category of a stored item, from the items database (or the id alone when the
    30	    database is not given or does not hold it)."""
    31	    cache = {}
    32	
    33	    def item_of(input_id):
    34	        if input_id not in cache:
    35	            row = items_db.execute('select title, publisher, publisher_type, category, publication_day, source_uri from items where input_id=?', (input_id,)).fetchone() if items_db is not None else None
    36	            cache[input_id] = dict(row) if row else {'title': input_id, 'publisher': '', 'publisher_type': '', 'category': '', 'publication_day': '', 'source_uri': ''}
    37	        return cache[input_id]
    38	    return item_of
